    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.bracketed\n\n### Description\n\nAwesome plugins! :sunglasses: \r\n\r\nI find `[j` and `]j` - jumping around the jumplist within the current buffer very useful! \r\n\r\nIt would be great if a complementary feature is implemented to jump around the different open buffers in the sequence of the jumplist. \r\n\r\nIt could maybe be implemented in the existing functions:\r\n- `oldfile` with an option not to reopen closed files, and limit itself to the current session only,\r\n- `buffer` if it can go through them historically rather than the buffer list. ",
