        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks again for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nWith the release of [mini.visits](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-visits.md), I think the suggestion from this issue will somewhat duplicate functionality. Although 'mini.visits' operates only on file paths and not precise positions in them, the suggestion in intended usage is very to close to \"jump to previous file that is not a current buffer\". I would like to avoid duplication in 'mini.nvim' as much as reasonably possible.\r\n\r\nClosing with suggestion to try 'mini.visits' for this type of functionality.",
