        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Ok thanks 🙏 \n\nGoing through your code here it seems that you iterate through files in the current directory? This won't work if you have buffers open from different non-nested directories?\n\nAlso, does `mini.visits` jump to the last location in that buffer?\n\nI was thinking more of iterating through the jumplist until a buffer that is not the current buffer is reached.\n\nThis could be done with a small mod of your existing function `is_jump_num_from_current_buffer`:\n```lua\n  local is_jump_num_not_from_current_buffer = function(jump_num)\n    local jump_entry = jump_list[jump_num]\n    if jump_entry == nil then return end\n    return jump_entry.bufnr ~= cur_buf_id\n  end\n```\nbtw kudos for the naming - really easy to go through the code! 👏 \n\nI could go for a PR if it's ok?",
