        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I was thinking as a copy of `jump()` say `jump_between_buffers()`.\n\nThat is definitely out of scope, I am afraid. For the reasons described in previous comment (no good key + technically a breaking change) but also because it is even more added lines and complexity than custom option.\n\nIf you *need* to use jumplist exactly and suggested 'mini.visits' approach is not good enough, then I'd suggest writing custom target by mostly copying [`MiniBracketed.jump()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ecde5ffd9adfd590d5c2d5d35a7f0152def894fc/lua/mini/bracketed.lua#L661). It is not a huge function to begin with and it can be made smaller after removing some safe guards needed for a general function in a plugin.",
